---
// Home. Adapted from: 10-Projects\bndy-website\home.md.
// Structure per spec §4 and design D: hero, marquee, belief rows, statement, stub teaser, close, doors.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Logo from '../components/Logo.astro';
import Marquee from '../components/Marquee.astro';
import Doors from '../components/Doors.astro';
import { MAP_URL, STAGE_LOGIN_URL, SITE_URL } from '../config';

const organization = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Organization',
  name: 'bndy',
  url: `${SITE_URL}/`,
  logo: `${SITE_URL}/og-card.png`,
  slogan: 'Keeping live music alive',
  description:
    'bndy helps people find grassroots live music near them: pubs, clubs, bars, back rooms, small stages and local venues. Built for the gigs everybody else misses.',
};
---
<Base
  title="bndy · Keeping live music alive"
  description="Find live music near you. Tonight, this weekend, wherever you are. bndy is built for the gigs everybody else misses. No ticket required."
  path="/"
  structuredData={organization}
>
  <header class="hero hero-with-bg">
    <picture class="hero-bg">
      <source media="(max-width: 768px)" srcset="/images/bndy_landing_banner_mobile.jpg" />
      <img src="/images/bndy_landing_banner.jpg" alt="" loading="eager" />
    </picture>
    <div class="hero-bg-overlay"></div>
    <div class="beams"></div>
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <Logo class="hero-logo" label="bndy" />
      <h1 class="strap">Keeping <span class="live">LIVE</span> Music <span class="alive">ALIVE</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub"><b>Find live music near you. Tonight, this weekend, wherever you are.</b></p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={MAP_URL}>Open the map</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={STAGE_LOGIN_URL}>Backstage login</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-note">no account needed to look · artists and venues sign in to Backstage</div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <Marquee />

  <section class="beliefs" id="beliefs">
    <div class="beliefs-head reveal"><h2 class="tight">What we believe</h2><span class="mono">SET 1 OF 1</span></div>

    <div class="row reveal-left stagger-1">
      <div class="row-no">01</div>
      <h3 class="tight">Live music doesn't start in arenas</h3>
      <div class="row-body">
        <p>It starts in pubs, clubs, bars, back rooms, small stages and local venues. With bands playing because they love it, venues taking a chance, and people deciding to go out rather than stay in.</p>
        <p>That's the bit of live music we care about.</p>
        <p><Logo class="inline-logo" label="bndy" /> exists to help people find it.</p>
        <p>No matter how small the gig.<br />No matter whether there's a ticket.<br />No matter whether the artist has 50 followers or 50,000.</p>
        <p><span class="em">If it's live music, it deserves to be found.</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row reveal-right stagger-1">
      <div class="row-no">02</div>
      <h3 class="tight">Most gigs aren't on the big ticket sites</h3>
      <div class="row-body">
        <p>There are thousands of gigs happening every week that never appear on the big music platforms.</p>
        <p>Because there's nothing to sell.</p>
        <p>A new originals band playing a free pub gig doesn't generate a booking fee. An acoustic night in a local bar isn't interesting to a ticketing company. A covers band playing a packed little venue might barely exist online outside a Facebook post.</p>
        <p>But these gigs matter.</p>
        <p>They give original artists somewhere to be heard.<br />They keep working bands playing.<br />They keep venues open.<br />They get people out.<br />They create scenes.</p>
        <p><span class="em"><Logo class="inline-logo" label="bndy" /> is built for the gigs everybody else misses.</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row reveal-left stagger-1">
      <div class="row-no">03</div>
      <h3 class="tight">Free doesn't mean less important</h3>
      <div class="row-body">
        <p>A gig doesn't become more valuable because somebody put a £25 ticket on it.</p>
        <p>Some of the best nights happen in places where you simply walk through the door.</p>
        <p>So <Logo class="inline-logo" label="bndy" /> treats free-to-attend live music as first-class live music.</p>
        <p>Not filler.<br />Not an afterthought.<br />Not something buried underneath ticketed events.</p>
        <p>It's at the heart of what we're building.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row reveal-right stagger-1">
      <div class="row-no">04</div>
      <h3 class="tight">The scene belongs to the people in it</h3>
      <div class="row-body">
        <p>The bands. The venues. The promoters. The people who turn up.</p>
        <p><Logo class="inline-logo" label="bndy" /> isn't here to put a tollbooth in the middle of that.</p>
        <p>Anyone can send a gig to <Logo class="inline-logo" label="bndy" />. BNDY Curators help discover artists, venues and gigs in the places they actually know because they're part of those local scenes.</p>
        <p>Automation helps us search further. People bring the local knowledge.</p>
        <p>We're here to connect what already exists, make it easier to discover, and help more people through the door.</p>
        <p><b>The technology should serve the scene.</b></p>
        <p><b>Not the other way around.</b></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row reveal-left stagger-1">
      <div class="row-no">05</div>
      <h3 class="tight">You shouldn't have to know where to look</h3>
      <div class="row-body">
        <p>Finding local music is weirdly difficult.</p>
        <p>One venue posts on Facebook. Another uses Instagram. A band puts its dates on its website. Somebody else posts a flyer into a local group. Another gig only appears on a listings site you've never heard of.</p>
        <p>You shouldn't need to follow 40 venues and 100 bands just to work out what's happening on Saturday night.</p>
        <p>That's our job.</p>
        <p><Logo class="inline-logo" label="bndy" /> searches, connects and organises the fragmented world of grassroots live music, while artists, venues, gig-goers and Curators help fill the gaps technology will always miss.</p>
        <p>So you can simply open the map and see what's happening around you.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row reveal-right stagger-1">
      <div class="row-no">06</div>
      <h3 class="tight">The map starts with where you are</h3>
      <div class="row-body">
        <p>Most music platforms start with an artist.</p>
        <p>We start with you.</p>
        <p>Open <Logo class="inline-logo" label="bndy" /> and look around.</p>
        <p>Tonight. Tomorrow. This weekend.<br />Walkable. A short drive. Somewhere worth going.</p>
        <p>Because sometimes you don't know which band you want to see.</p>
        <p>You just know you fancy seeing a band.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row reveal-left stagger-1">
      <div class="row-no">07</div>
      <h3 class="tight">We measure success in people turning up</h3>
      <div class="row-body">
        <p>Not time spent in the app.<br />Not endless scrolling.<br />Not notifications designed to drag you back.</p>
        <p>If <Logo class="inline-logo" label="bndy" /> helps you find a band you've never heard of, walk into a venue you've never visited and have a brilliant night, it worked.</p>
        <p><span class="em">The objective isn't to keep you in <Logo class="inline-logo" label="bndy" />. It's to get you out to a gig.</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="statement reveal-scale">
    <h2 class="tight">NO TICKET REQUIRED.</h2>
    <p>Some of the most important live music in Britain happens without one.</p>
    <p>Ticketed gigs already have an internet built around them. Free and low-cost gigs often don't.</p>
    <p><b><Logo class="inline-logo" label="bndy" /> looks hardest where ticketing doesn't.</b></p>
  </section>

  <section class="stub-wrap reveal" id="promise">
    <div class="stub">
      <div class="stub-main">
        <div class="k">Our promise</div>
        <h3 class="tight">We won't hide gigs because nobody paid us.</h3>
        <p>We won't make artists pay to exist. We won't make venues pay to exist. Ticketed gigs still belong here, but we'll put our effort where the discovery problem is hardest. Eight promises, in writing, no small print.</p>
        <a href="/promise">Read our promise →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="stub-side">
        <div class="no tight">No ticket<br />required</div>
        <div class="adm">Admit everyone</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="close-section reveal">
    <p>Go to gigs. Try a band you've never heard of. Walk into a venue you've never visited.</p>
    <p><b>We'll help you find it. The rest is up to all of us.</b></p>
    <div class="close-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={MAP_URL}>Open the map</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/why">Read why we're building this →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Doors />
</Base>
